e allowed immediate comparison, the remote branch matched the new commit while the PR API still reported the prior head `8b23aaa087b60844c63459a1c625a23dc954ba03`; this round must establish current live state independently.\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4e6ca57487d089f20d77b64f526a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b4f9-6008-7481-8c13-f3c8d9cbf433"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning selective ledger reading before snapshot**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_fdyWUN7EbEUPawd73jr6jTSv","id":"ctc_05349b17f5ad9d6a016aad4e6ef88887d0919bca2c3b47e5dd","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"sed -n '80,220p' .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\\nsed -n '221,410p' .conduct/pr-170-remediation-ledger.md\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/PR-170\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 50000\n});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789742699.604659,"turn_id":"01a0b4f9-6008-7481-8c13-f3c8d9cbf433"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_fdyWUN7EbEUPawd73jr6jTSv","id":"ctco_01a0b4fa-6f0e-7231-af45-0cef2f16730c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789742706.446736,"turn_id":"01a0b4f9-6008-7481-8c13-f3c8d9cbf433"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 11377)\nTotal output lines: 331\n\n\n### Round 8 reset-trigger reassessment\n\n- Shared invariant: every target-controlled value that occupies authored report structure must be proven unchanged by the active live-session redactor before emission; a structural collision must make the report safely incomplete. Every post-execution conformance output or persistence failure is an operational failure with fixed safe text and exit 1, while an existing retryable cleanup owner remains authoritative.\n- Producers / consumers: custom targets produce arbitrary `describe().kind` values and target-owned redaction; the live `McpFnClient` owns the active redactor and structural-preservation check; the target suite reconstructs bounded JSON/JUnit artifacts consumed by libraries and `mcpfn test-target`. Official conformance produces captured streams and bounded reports consumed by `runCli`, stdout/stderr callbacks, and report persistence.\n- Failure boundaries: suite projection after scenario execution but before credential cleanup; reinsertion of the raw target discriminator after descriptor payload redaction; final JSON/JUnit serialization; conformance stdout/stderr callbacks and report-file writes; cleanup-owner priority over secondary I/O failures.\n- Coordinated repair: validate the dynamic target kind with the live client's shared `preserveArtifactStructure` enforcement before reconstructing the descriptor so a collision sets the existing projection-failure path; apply the existing cleanup-aware safe runtime-output wrapper to the complete conformance stdout/stderr/report operation with a conformance-specific fixed message.\n- Verification criteria: a custom target whose redactor treats its arbitrary kind as a credential must return a bounded incomplete report with the raw kind absent; conformance report, stdout, and stderr failures without a cleanup owner must return exit 1 with fixed safe text and omit raw I/O details, while the existing cleanup-owner priority regressions remain green. Then affected package tests/typechecks/builds, the complete Node 22 release gate, `git diff --check`, and whole-batch caller review.\n\n## Defect-family ledger\n\n| Stable ID | Root cause / affected contract | Disposition | First seen | Last attempted | Attempted repairs | Regression / verification evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `MCP170-CREDENTIAL-BOUNDARY` | Credential-safe redaction across reconstructed targets, diagnostics, and emitted artifacts | Fixed in round 7 batch; recurring family | pre-ledger | round 7 | Prior `1e45b794…` plus round 7 structured-Cookie component extraction/fail-closed parsing | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvkZ0`; direct reflected Cookie values are now removed and ambiguous syntax is rejected; testing suite and release gate pass |\n| `MCP170-CLEANUP-PHASE` | Dynamic revoke/dispose cleanup phase and safe CLI failure handling | Fixed in round 7 batch; recurring family | pre-ledger | round 7 | Prior `1e45b794…` and `a9fc7f4b…`; round 7 preserves the safe release rejection through target-level pre-handle cleanup retries | Threads `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvje4` and `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jv3uO`; failed-open OAuth cleanup remains `token-revocation` / `authorization-server` and the retry owner succeeds later |\n| `MCP170-CLEANUP-OWNER` | Retryable suite/test/conformance cleanup errors must retain their owning client/lease through `runCli`; only `bin.ts` may terminate, after a diagnostic is flushed | Fixed locally; recurring family | pre-ledger | round 1 | Prior `1e45b794…` fixed some paths; round 1 persists reports, propagates all owning errors, retries at the library boundary, and flushes executable diagnostics | Four current comments deduplicate to this root cause; CLI regressions prove report persistence and a second caller-owned retry after the bounded retry fails |\n| `MCP170-SNAPSHOT-PAYLOAD-MODE` | Inspector standalone descriptor/server/capability/inventory projections must use payload redaction, not envelope preservation | Fixed locally; recurring credential-boundary sibling | pre-ledger | round 1 | Round 1 passes `preserveKeys: false` for all snapshot projections | Two current comments deduplicate to this root cause; mode-sensitive snapshot regression passes |\n| `MCP170-OAUTH-TOKEN-CACHE` | Successful exchange and refresh responses must have a JSON media type and both mandated non-cache headers | Fixed locally | round 1 | round 1 | Round 1 validates both directives and adds them to hosted and mock producers | Exchange/refresh regressions cover each missing directive; auth and testing suites pass |\n| `MCP170-TEST-EVIDENCE` | Regression fixtures must not claim retry behavior they cannot exercise | Fixed locally | round 1 | round 1 | Removed dead `connectRetries` from the initialization-cleanup regression | One current comment. The separate key-redaction assertion comment was disproved by execution: `${MCPFN_SECRET}` is credential-shaped and its associated value is intentionally redacted |\n| `MCP170-CI-SUPPLYCHAIN` | Python bootstrap in the required CI workflow must install wheel-only packages | Fixed; round 2 Sonar snapshot successful | round 1 | round 1 | Added `--only-binary :all:` to the pip/build upgrade step | Sonar security rating failed in round 1; round 2 SonarCloud Code Analysis and Quality Gate passed |\n| `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` | External analyzer inventory contains 36 additional maintainability/reliability findings | Not Attempted (non-gating broad refactor inventory); preserve for reassessment | round 1 | not attempted | None | Round 4 Sonar Quality Gate passed, but its summary increased from 35 to 36 open issues; individual analyzer details were not part of the captured GitHub review surfaces and require a separately coordinated behavior-preserving assessment |\n| `MCP170-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION` | Registered credential variants must not be silently exempted when they collide with authored artifact discriminator values | Fixed locally; recurring credential-boundary sibling | round 2 | round 2 | Shared scrubber now rejects structural-value collisions while retaining fixed schema keys; suite callers convert the failure to a non-passing incomplete artifact | `pass`, `complete`, target-kind, side-effect and version collisions fail closed; 113 focused testing regressions pass |\n| `MCP170-CONFORMANCE-CAP` | A size-truncated official conformance artifact must be explicitly incomplete and non-passing | Fixed locally | round 2 | round 2 | Bounded serializer records `status: incomplete`, an explicit reason, `ok: false`, and exit 1 | Oversized-success regression persists within 1025 bytes and returns exit 1 |\n| `MCP170-CLI-OUTPUT-DRAIN` | Cleanup-owner propagation to `bin.ts` must not force-exit before queued stdout evidence is flushed | Fixed locally; cleanup-owner sibling | round 2 | round 2 | CLI output callbacks may be async; default process writes resolve on their callbacks; every call site awaits completion | Delayed-stdout regression proves the cleanup retry does not begin until stdout resolves; CLI suite and release gate pass |\n| `MCP170-CLEANUP-EVIDENCE` | Cleanup leak regression must inspect non-enumerable error text as well as the enumerable report | Fixed locally | round 2 | round 2 | Assertion checks `error.message` and `JSON.stringify(error.report)` separately | Focused suite regression passes and distinguishes the previously unobserved field |\n| `MCP170-CLEANUP-OWNER-PRIORITY` | Conformance/target cleanup ownership must survive later report, stdout, stderr, and diagnostic failures | Fixed and pushed; recurring cleanup-owner family | round 3 | round 3 | `9371beeb…`: cleanup-aware output/persistence wrapper preserves the owner; outer diagnostics are best-effort before the bounded retry | Two current comments deduplicate to this root cause; output and persistence replacement regressions pass for conformance and target suites |\n| `MCP170-INSPECT-CLEANUP-OWNER` | Inspector close failures must retain a retryable client/transport owner through `runCli` and `bin.ts` | Fixed and pushed; recurring cleanup-owner family | round 3 | round 3 | `9371beeb…`: retained `McpFnInspectorCleanupError`, bounded library retry, and executable-boundary classification | Inspector regression proves two failed closes retain the owner and a later caller retry closes successfully |\n| `MCP170-OAUTH-PUBLIC-CLIENT-STATUS` | Unauthenticated public-client token exchange/refresh `invalid_client` rejection must require HTTP 400, not accept a 401 client-authentication challenge | Fixed and pushed | round 3 | round 3 | `9371beeb…`: token rejection validation now requires HTTP 400 for all public-client errors | Exchange and refresh regressions pass at 400 and fail envelope validation at 401; requests assert no Authorization header |\n| `MCP170-INSPECTOR-STRUCTURAL-COLLISION` | Direct client/inspector artifacts reconstruct discriminator values after payload redaction and can expose an equal credential | Fixed and pushed; recurring credential-boundary family | round 4 | round 4 | `afcf360f…`: shared client structural-safety enforcement covers events/diagnostics and inspector snapshots/scenarios; omission counters preserve evidence when no safe envelope can be emitted | One current thread names `clientState`; regressions cover authenticated state, target/root kinds, event/diagnostic kinds, scenario kind/side effect, reports, and mixed ESM/CJS consumers |\n| `MCP170-TEST-CLIENT-CLOSE-OWNER` | A successfully connected `McpFnTestClient` can lose its retained session when public `close()` fails | Fixed and pushed; recurring cleanup-owner family | round 4 | round 4 | `afcf360f…`: public `close()` returns the existing retryable owner; target-suite composition retains that exact inner owner | One current thread; regression proves two failed close attempts keep the same owner and a later retry succeeds; CLI owner tests and release gate pass |\n| `MCP170-TIMESTAMP-STRUCTURE` | Credential redaction can turn generated client/diagnostic ISO timestamps into malformed consumer-visible values | Fixed and pushed; recurring credential-boundary family | round 5 | round 5 | `30e7ff8e…`: safe exact ISO timestamps are enforced at the shared client producer and collisions use omission accounting | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jutb6`; exact-collision and no-safe-ISO regressions pass, as does the full release gate |\n| `MCP170-CLEANUP-ERROR-SANITIZATION` | Raw provider revoke/dispose or target cleanup errors can escape through public client cause chains | Fixed in round 7 batch; cleanup/credential-boundary sibling | round 7 | round 7 | Lease and client cleanup wrappers retain safe fixed text, phase, and retryability without attaching raw cleanup causes | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvjew`; direct lease and client regressions prove provider secrets are absent and public cleanup causes are undefined |\n| `MCP170-STRUCTURED-CREDENTIAL-REDACTION` | Cookie credential components may reflect independently of the complete request header | Fixed in round 7 batch; credential-boundary sibling | round 7 | round 7 | Shared credential discovery extracts unquoted and quoted Cookie values and rejects ambiguous structured syntax | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvkZ0`; direct redaction regressions distinguish the previously leaking values |\n| `MCP170-CLI-RUNTIME-OUTPUT` | Target-suite JSON, JUnit, or stdout failures after execution are misclassified as CLI usage errors | Fixed in round 7 batch | round 7 | round 7 | Target-suite output boundary now raises a safe `McpFnClientError` when no cleanup owner exists and still prioritizes a retained owner | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jvkZ9`; output/JUnit/stdout regressions return exit 1 with fixed safe text and existing owner-priority tests remain green |\n| `MCP170-TARGET-KIND-STRUCTURE` | A custom target's arbitrary `describe().kind` can be reinserted raw after descriptor redaction and expose target-owned credential material | Fixed and pushed; recurring credential-boundary family | round 8 | round 8 | `dfaeef0d1…`: validate the dynamic kind through the connected client's shared structural-preservation enforcement and fail the projection closed on collision while preserving the established incomplete-reason contract | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwTTA`; focused regression proves the raw kind is absent and the bounded report is incomplete |\n| `MCP170-CONFORMANCE-RUNTIME-OUTPUT` | Conformance stdout, stderr, or report persistence failures after execution are misclassified as CLI usage errors | Fixed and pushed; recurring CLI runtime-output family | round 8 | round 8 | `dfaeef0d1…`: supply a fixed safe conformance failure message to the cleanup-aware output wrapper without weakening cleanup-owner priority | Thread `PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6jwTTI`; report/stdout/stderr regressions return exit 1 and omit raw callback/filesystem details |\n\n## Round 1 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 8 unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 4 code/test root causes, plus 1 Sonar required-check root cause. All five root causes are fixed by `45785a27458b9f42e20e1fc3023489a0a7d3998d`; the captured threads were not resolved or refetched.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 71 unresolved GitHub threads (29 current-hunk and 42 outdated-hunk) trace to current implementations/tests that already enforce the reported behavior. Outdated status was not used as proof; current producer/consumer paths were inspected.\n- Not Attempted: the 35 non-gating Sonar maintainability/reliability findings remain recorded under `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY`; no GitHub review item is unassessed.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 GitHub comment is invalid based on the passing observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks. Analyzer `throw this` findings target classes extending `Error`; the reported Basic-token regex operates only after the 8 KiB credential-value bound, so these specific diagnostics are not unbounded runtime defects.\n- Unassessed: 0 GitHub review threads; 0 supplementary review bodies/comments.\n\n## Round 1 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: 17 check contexts were terminal: 13 successful, 1 failed (SonarCloud security rating), 1 neutral, and 2 skipped. `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted in this round.\n\n## Round 1 convergence\n\n- Trend: improving locally: five selected blocking root-cause families were repaired and verified, but the round is not clean because it changed/pushed the head, the only allowed check snapshot predates the push and contained a failure, and one broad non-gating analyzer-maintainability family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 5 / 1 deferred non-gating analyzer-maintainability family; all selected functional and required-check root causes are fixed locally.\n- New defects: OAuth token cache-envelope validation, inaccurate regression evidence, and CI wheel-only bootstrap.\n- Recurring families: cleanup ownership and credential payload redaction.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none found after whole-batch review and the release gate. One reviewer claim about an incorrect authenticated-artifact assertion was disproved by execution and classified Invalid.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: broad Sonar maintainability inventory from the PR's earlier commits; security-rating failure is selected for this round because it is the only reported failed gate condition.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by actionable findings, a code change/push, the changed PR head, the failed immediate check snapshot, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: snapshot collection was stable at `1e45b794d946722409dc86681a1ee9a34bfe7f2f`; the authorized round then advanced local/remote/PR head together to `45785a27458b9f42e20e1fc3023489a0a7d3998d`.\n\n## Round 1 verification evidence\n\n- Focused: 35 client tests, 28 inspector authenticated-artifact tests, 50 hosted-authorization/mock-server tests, and 37 CLI tests passed.\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/auth`, `@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/testing`, `@mcpfn/inspector`, and `@mcpfn/cli` passed.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed after rebuilding the locked `better-sqlite3` native binding that `npm ci --ignore-scripts` intentionally omitted. The first attempt reached all affected McpFn stages successfully before that unrelated bootstrap failure.\n- Gate coverage included full package tests/builds, Playwright, official conformance, examples, mixed-entry redaction, ESM/CJS imports, package dry-runs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state was not refetched or polled after edits; only the recorded immediate snapshot may be reported.\n\n## Round 2 snapshot dispositions\n\n- Actionable at snapshot: 4 new unresolved GitHub threads, deduplicated to 4 root causes. All four are fixed in the reviewed local batch; threads were not resolved and review surfaces will not be refetched after push.\n- Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale): 75 older unresolved threads retain round 1 current-code evidence because the assessed head is exactly the round 1 pushed head and the affected implementations are unchanged outside this batch.\n- Invalid / Accepted Risk: 1 older GitHub finding remains invalid based on observed key-redaction behavior; no accepted risks.\n- Not Attempted: the Sonar summary still reports 35 open maintainability/reliability findings although its Quality Gate passed. The family remains deferred and visible; individual analyzer findings were not substituted for the captured review snapshot or declared fixed.\n- Unassessed: 0 captured GitHub threads, review bodies, issue comments, or inline comments.\n\n## Round 2 required-check snapshot\n\n- One snapshot only: 18 contexts comprised 11 successful, 2 in progress (CodeQL Swift and Pullfrog), 2 neutral, and 3 skipped. SonarCloud and Cubic were successful; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\n\n## Round 2 convergence\n\n- Trend: improving locally but non-clean. Four newly discovered root causes are repaired and verified, while the captured hosted snapshot had two pending checks and the 35-item analyzer family remains deferred.\n- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code/test root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: structural credential collisions, falsely passing truncated conformance artifacts, unawaited CLI evidence writes, and incomplete cleanup leak assertions.\n- Recurring families: credential boundary and cleanup ownership/output delivery.\n- Fix-induced regressions: none after updating superseded structural-collision expectations and running the full release gate.\n- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1; the current Sonar quality gate is successful but the captured summary still lists 35 open issues.\n- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new findings, recurring-family evidence, this code-changing round, two pending hosted checks, and the deferred analyzer family).\n- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `45785a27458b9f42e20e1fc3023489a0a7d3998d`; the authorized round then advanced local, remote, and PR head together to `eda8c5b01fa394e35174a88a6bdca078d793ec8c` in the one allowed comparison.\n\n## Round 2 verification evidence\n\n- Focused testing: 113 `@mcpfn/testing` regressions and 11 `@mcpfn/cli` cleanup/cap regressions passed.\n- Typechecks: `@mcpfn/testing` and `@mcpfn/cli` passed.\n- Release gate: `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release` passed all package tests/builds, Playwright, official conformance, mixed-entry redaction, examples, ESM/CJS imports, package dry-runs, packed-consumer installation, and round trips.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Hosted CI/reviewer state will not be refetched or polled after this snapshot.\n\n## Round 2 termination\n\n- Result: nonterminal recurring run; automation remains enabled for a future separately scheduled assessment.\n- No post-push review refetch, CI poll, reviewer wait, thread resolutio…1377 tokens truncated…after: 2 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\n- New defects: direct structural credential collisions in client/inspector artifacts and lost post-connect test-client cleanup ownership; the Sonar summary also reports one additional