l: 14 successful, 1 neutral, and 3 skipped. There were no pending or failed contexts; `reviewDecision` was empty. No check polling is permitted.\\n+\\n+## Round 9 convergence\\n+\\n+- Trend: stalled across scheduled convergence. Four selected roots are repaired locally, but credential-boundary and CLI runtime-output families recurred and the 36-finding analyzer family remains deferred.\\n+- Valid blocking root causes before / after: 4 selected code root causes plus 1 deferred analyzer family / 1 deferred analyzer family.\\n+- New defects: false credential-failure taxonomy for hostile descriptors, classified runtime failure replacement by persistent stderr rejection, fixed-key credential leakage, and unvalidated event/diagnostic target descriptors.\\n+- Recurring families: credential-boundary structural safety and CLI runtime-output classification recurred; the reset-trigger assessment repaired shared producer boundaries before mutation.\\n+- Fix-induced regressions: none remain. The first focused testing run exposed two incorrect new test expectations; the expectations were corrected to distinguish recoverable discriminator-value omission from unrecoverable fixed-key collision, after which all focused suites and the complete release gate passed.\\n+- Oldest deferred blocker: `MCP170-SONAR-MAINTAINABILITY` from round 1, last observed at 36 findings. It remains Not Attempted and prevents a clean assessment despite terminal successful required checks.\\n+- Clean streak: `0` (reset by four actionable/new root causes, recurring families, this code-changing round, and the deferred analyzer family).\\n+- Head stability: the complete snapshot stayed at `dfaeef0d1a4b25cc2ae9e10ccde0481b255637ad`; the one allowed local/remote/PR comparison remains pending until after the authorized push.\\n+\\n+## Round 9 verification evidence\\n+\\n+- Focused testing: all 41 `@mcpfn/client` tests, 121 target-suite/remote-target `@mcpfn/testing` tests, and 15 conformance-cleanup `@mcpfn/cli` 